================================================================================
                           THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTIONS
================================================================================

This Software integrates with, but does NOT include, the following third-party
components. Users must obtain these components separately and comply with their
respective licenses and copyrights:

1. SHAW MODEL (Simultaneous Heat and Water)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Copyright: United States Department of Agriculture (USDA), Agricultural
              Research Service (ARS)
   Original Developer: Dr. Gerald N. Flerchinger
   Institution: USDA-ARS Northwest Watershed Research Center, Boise, Idaho
   Status: U.S. Government work (public domain in the United States)
   Source: https://www.ars.usda.gov/pacific-west-area/boise-id/
          northwest-watershed-research-center/docs/shaw-model/
   Download: ftp://ftp.nwrc.ars.usda.gov/public/ShawModel/

   The SHAW model is NOT included in this repository. Users must download
   the model directly from the official USDA-ARS source. The SHAW model is
   a U.S. Government work and is not subject to copyright protection in the
   United States, but may be subject to copyright in other jurisdictions.

2. ESMDA ALGORITHM (Ensemble Smoother with Multiple Data Assimilation)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Copyright: Alexandre A. Emerick and Albert C. Reynolds
   Institution: The University of Tulsa, Petroleum Reservoir Exploitation
                Projects
   Original Publications:
     - Emerick, A.A. and Reynolds, A.C. (2013). "Ensemble smoother with
       multiple data assimilation." Computers & Geosciences, 55, 3-15.
       DOI: 10.1016/j.cageo.2012.03.011
     - Emerick, A.A. and Reynolds, A.C. (2012). "History matching time-lapse
       seismic data using the ensemble Kalman smoother with multiple data
       assimilation." Computational Geosciences, 16(3), 639-659.
       DOI: 10.1007/s10596-012-9275-5

   The ESMDA implementation in this Software is an independent Python
   re-implementation based on the published mathematical formulations.
   The original algorithm and its theoretical foundation remain the
   intellectual property of Emerick and Reynolds.

3. ILUES ALGORITHM (Iterative Local Updating Ensemble Smoother)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Copyright: Dr. Jiangjiang Zhang (张江江) and co-authors
   Institution: Hohai University (河海大学), Yangtze Institute for Conservation
                and Development, Nanjing, China
   Original Publication:
     - Zhang, J., Lin, G., Li, W., Zeng, L., and Wu, L. (2018). "An iterative
       local updating ensemble smoother for estimation and uncertainty
       assessment of hydrologic model parameters with multimodal distributions."
       Water Resources Research, 54(3), 1716-1733.
       DOI: 10.1002/2017WR021296
   Preprint: arXiv:1611.04702 [stat.CO]
   Contact: zhangjiangjiang@hhu.edu.cn

   The ILUES implementation in this Software is an independent Python
   re-implementation based on the published mathematical formulations.
   The original algorithm and its theoretical foundation remain the
   intellectual property of Dr. Jiangjiang Zhang and co-authors.

